# Fan Fold — third-party notices

Fan Fold is a Linux desktop notes application written in Qt 6, QML and C++ for
KDE Plasma 6. The application itself is original work; the components below are
included under their own licences.

## Bundled components

- **Vditor** Markdown editor, vendored at `third_party/vditor-3.11.2/`.
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2019-present B3log 开源, b3log.org. The complete
  license text is included at
  [`third_party/vditor-3.11.2/LICENSE`](third_party/vditor-3.11.2/LICENSE).
  The vendored distribution includes its own bundled dependencies (for example
  highlight.js styles and diff-match-patch) under their respective licenses,
  enumerated in the packaged `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.

## Colour palette values

Fan Fold ships 25 curated note palettes. Each one reuses exact published colour
values from the source named below; the palette arrangement, the ink-contrast
derivation and the paper/ink pairing are original to this project.

The in-application palette picker shows the same attribution and licence for
whichever palette is selected, so credit travels with the software.

### Original to this project

**Pastels** and **Grayscale** — original, licensed under the terms of this
repository.

### ColorBrewer 2.0 — Apache License 2.0

**Bold**, **Muted**, **Light**, **Pastel**, **Soft**, **Deep**, **Paired** and
**Highlight** use the qualitative schemes Set1, Set2, Set3, Pastel1, Pastel2,
Dark2, Paired and Accent from ColorBrewer 2.0 (colorbrewer2.org), by Cynthia
Brewer, Mark Harrower and The Pennsylvania State University.

